# Riverglades for the Horde, part 1 of 4 (2026-11-12; the Horde route since 0.4.0). Hand-written from players'
# recordings of the zone (123 sessions to 2026-11-12) and Forever's quest data (the client's quest records,
# QuestieDB 1.0.16 and EG Link) for titles, levels, objectives and places.
# Order: the way in on foot from Kargath through Twilight's Shroud (after the Stranglethorn Vale & Swamp of Sorrows
# guide, about level 42: a flight from Stonard to Kargath, then Rog'mar first and Sleebo's workshop), or by the goblin
# boat from Tanaris for a character without Kargath's flight path (Powderfuse Port, Sleebo's workshop, then Rog'mar);
# Rog'mar (flight path, inn), Neza Bloodsnout's three hunts on the plains with Sleebo's marsh on the first one, a western loop
# (Turner's Logging Camp, the Bristle Hills, Gelinda Coppergleam's Cinderscale hollow, Meadowsbrook) and the hearth
# home, the training grounds, then the river and the Farholde training camp.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (players' recordings): Poison Tips after Feathers for Fletching,
# A Hunter's Quiver after Poison Tips, Gnoll Infestation, Bristle Hills Bandits and Snargl's Snout after A Hunter's
# Quiver; A Gift From Our Enemies after Food for the Taking; Show Them How It's Done after both of Krom'rosh's first
# quests; A Serving of Strength after A Gift From Our Enemies; Stick 'Em after Fetch 'n' Fletch; The Goblin Trader
# after Borrowed Blades; Rock 'em and Sock 'em after Gaseous Gold; Tran'gul's quests after Show Them How It's Done
# (part 2).
# Elites, each behind a group choice: Snargl (40), Ombassa (41), Ghostmaw (42); Scoutmaster Vargas (42) in part 2.
# Picked up on the way here: Report to Rog'mar (95141, Commander Aggro'gosh at Grom'gol, in the Stranglethorn Vale
# guide). Taken here for the next guide: On the Other Side (95033, Tan'jani, for Camp Mojache) and Shipping and
# Handling (95296, Friz, for Steamwheedle Port), both on the Feralas & Tanaris guide's way.
# Twice Misplaced Trust (97332): Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay offers it after Anything of Value (97328) and
#   Zimmix's Great Escape (97331), both done in the 30-40 Stranglethorn guide; the Stranglethorn Vale guide's first
#   Booty Bay stop takes it and Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz takes it on the first port stop here.
# Left out on purpose:
# - Hail the Dragonslayer (95936): it starts from the head of Scaldaron, a rare elite drake in the Cinderscale
#   hollow.
# - Finding Tan'jani (95143), from Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands: this guide doesn't assume you carry it;
#   While-you're-here hands it in when you have it.

step Fly to Kargath
  when taxi "Kargath"
  when zone "Swamp of Sorrows"
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  tip The Riverglades lie south of the Badlands. Ride east from the Harborage to Stonard and fly to Kargath: the way down into the zone starts there.
  goto 46.1,54.7 "Stonard flight master"
  fly "Kargath"
  zone Badlands

step Into the Riverglades
  when taxi "Kargath"
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  zone Badlands
  tip New in Forever: this guide follows what players did in the Riverglades. If a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip From Kargath, ride south-east across the Badlands to the zone's southern edge: the pass of Twilight's Shroud leads down into the Riverglades. Rog'mar, the Horde's fort, stands in the middle of the zone, east along the valley.
  goto 55.0,93.0 "Into the Riverglades"
  zone Riverglades
  enter "Riverglades" @32.0,29.9

step Fly to Freewind Post
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  tip New in Forever: this guide follows what players did in the Riverglades. If a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip The Riverglades lie across the sea from Tanaris: a goblin boat sails from Steamwheedle Port, north-east of Gadgetzan, to Powderfuse Port. Fly to Freewind Post in Thousand Needles and head south-east through the Shimmering Flats to Gadgetzan. (If you already know Kargath in the Badlands, the way in through Twilight's Shroud works too.)
  fly "Freewind Post"

step Gadgetzan
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  zone Tanaris
  tip Learn Gadgetzan's flight path: it saves the ride next time.
  getfp "Gadgetzan"

step Boat to Powderfuse Port
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  zone Tanaris
  tip Steamwheedle Port is on the coast north-east of Gadgetzan: wait on the pier for the goblin boat to Powderfuse Port.
  goto 67.57,23.1 "Boat to Powderfuse Port"

step Powderfuse Port
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  zone Riverglades
  tip New in Forever: if a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Friz Frazzlespark keeps a stall at the west end of the docks. The port's other jobs are for later in this guide: this crate goes to the Horde's fort.
  accept 95062                          -- Frazzlespark's Crate: for Krom'rosh in Rog'mar

step Sleebo's workshop
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  tip West up the road from the port: Sleebo Fizzlespout has his workshop on the hill. The gas vents are in the marsh south-west of it, on your first hunt for Neza.
  accept 96063                          -- Gaseous Gold

step Rog'mar
  tip West to Rog'mar, the Horde's fort in the middle of the zone. Neza Bloodsnout stands on its east side, Kreza Darkthorn and Krom'rosh in the middle with Grakna, the wind rider master; Innkeeper Toka and Tan'jani on the west side.
  accept 96107                          -- Neza Bloodsnout: Feathers for Fletching
  accept 93788                          -- Kreza Darkthorn: Borrowed Blades
  turnin 95141                          -- Krom'rosh: Aggro'gosh's report from Grom'gol, if you carry it
  accept 93786                          -- A Message in Blood
  accept 93787                          -- Food for the Taking
  getfp "Rog'mar" npc 255993            -- Grakna, in the middle of the fort
  sethome "Rog'mar" npc 256675         -- Innkeeper Toka
  accept 95951                          -- Tan'jani: Fetch 'n' Fletch
  accept 95033                          -- Tan'jani: On the Other Side, for Witch Doctor Uzer'i at Camp Mojache in the Feralas guide

